                     <watermark xml:id="watermark_65cd272b">centred at the top of the bifolio a watermark is partly visible consisting of the same bottom part of a beehive as the va. part; no countermark. Paper of a fairly dense quality.</watermark>
                     <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_5654274b">In 2<rend xml:id="idm91" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format; music (fols. 1r–2v); in all a single bifolio. Hand-ruled paper, 14 staves (10 mm; 14-stave (?) rastrum used) in light brown ink and music in black ink; bottom five staves on fol. 1v and a bottom stave on fol. 2r–v have not been used. A clean copy with few changes and corrections in ink; very few markings in pencil, presumably added in connection with a more recent transcription. Number of bars of each movement added at the final bars in red pencil, presumably of an earlier, most likely near-contemporary date.</physMedium>
                  </physDesc>
